  "open_questions": [
    {
      "id": "Q1",
      "question": "Should the qa package carry bound Python evaluation artifacts of its own? AGENTS.md names a JSONL runner, deterministic graders, fixtures, expected results, schema and digests as required build artifacts, and the source package's own QA-026 / QAP-014 clause states that qa's evaluated-build completeness requires exactly such a bundle. This conversion deliberately created no evals/, tests/ or scripts/, because skill-builder forbids generating evaluation campaigns during authoring and the validator package is documented as owning all quality campaigns. The maintainer must decide whether qa needs its own harness or whether validator ownership satisfies the requirement. This is the same unresolved question recorded as Q1 for the dev conversion.",
      "owner": "maintainer",
      "affected_behavior_ids": [
        "B8-assess-metrics-and-verdict"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q2",
      "question": "Should the converted skill be granted the Task tool? The source requires QA independence from development completion claims, which Claude Code could execute rather than merely assert by running verification in a fresh subagent context, as the legacy framework's ac-compliance-verifier did. Task is omitted here, applying the minimum grant; independence therefore remains a contract obligation of the single session rather than a context boundary the host enforces.",
      "owner": "maintainer",
      "affected_behavior_ids": [
        "B5-inspect-test-integrity",
        "B8-assess-metrics-and-verdict"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q3",
      "question": "Should the >=95% coverage and unit-test pass-rate floors remain written into references/assessment.md as the skill's own default? The adaptive design contrast states that DevForgeAI's thresholds should arrive as project-policy inputs rather than constants baked into a skill, yet the source states the floors directly and allows stricter project floors to override them. The converted package preserves the source wording unchanged; whether the floor should instead be supplied per project is a maintainer decision, not a conversion decision.",
      "owner": "maintainer",
      "affected_behavior_ids": [
        "B8-assess-metrics-and-verdict"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4",
      "question": "Does the ADR-073 mirror obligation apply to this package? CLAUDE.md states that .claude/ and src/claude/ are byte-identical copies and that any skill edit must be applied to both paths, and every sibling skill (advisor, dev, skill-builder, skill-validator) satisfies that today. The maintainer selected src/claude/skills/qa as the destination, and the dev conversion's own authoring record shows the .claude/ copy was made outside the authoring run. This run therefore writes only the selected target_root and reports the mirror as a separate pending action.",
      "owner": "maintainer",
      "affected_behavior_ids": [
        "B1-select-mode-and-scope"
      ]
    }
  ]
